      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict region_only: insert_after_residue 120 -> NULL; the paper names a region, not a junction (region: loop C at Thr-120 (junction 119|120 or 120|121 not stated)). Paper (PMID 7507481): \"The E1 epitope at Thr-120 was protease-sensitive in intact oocytes, indicating that loop C is exofacial.\". Audit note: Only the abstract was readable: JBC full text/PDF returned 403 to curl and a Cloudflare human-verification challenge in the browser (not completed); doi.org WebFetch was refused. The abstract names Thr-120 (T120 matches human CHIP28 canonical) but not whether the epitope is before/after/replacing it. Surface shown by chymotrypsin sensitivity in intact oocytes; the abstract reports biologically active channels except loop B/E insertions, implying water permeability was measured for the Thr-120 mutant. Species assumed human (Agre-lab CHIP28 cDNA), unverified.] L5 explicitly names Thr-120 as the insertion site and confirms extracellular display by protease sensitivity in intact oocytes. Python confirms T120 (residue 120 = T) in the canonical sequence, within EC2 (116\u2013135), 5 residues from the TM3 C-boundary (115) and 16 residues from the TM4 N-boundary (136), satisfying the \u22653-residue TM clearance requirement. 'Inserted at Thr-120' is interpreted as insert_after_residue=120 (tag between T120 and G121), placing the tag mid-loop with ample flanking space. A coronavirus E1 glycoprotein epitope was inserted at Thr-120 of full-length CHIP/AQP1 expressed in Xenopus oocytes. Protease (alpha-chymotrypsin) sensitivity in intact oocytes confirmed extracellular display of the epitope at this position, establishing loop C (EC2, residues 116\u2013135) as exofacial.",
